.env
.venv/
__pycache__/

# The account project's SECRET key never lives in a file here at all:
# dev/inbox.py reads it as DESKIT_SUPABASE_SECRET from the owner's own
# Windows user environment (plan 8.10), the product ships only the
# publishable key (sb.py), and nothing under this folder — not .env, not
# a settings file — is where it goes. The name is reserved here so it
# is never mistaken for one of the .env keys above.

# Everything below is a record of what you actually dictated — keep it off
# any remote. app.log holds the pasted text, pending\ holds raw audio,
# vocab.json holds words you said paired with what you meant, and
# lookup_cache.json is keyed by the literal text you selected and looked
# up — which is a record of what you were reading. (The seed terms in
# config.toml ARE committed — those are hand-written, not learned.)
transcripts.log*
app.log*
pending/
recent/
corpus/
vocab.json
vocab.json.bak-*
lookup_cache.json
# The second reading's proposals (review.py): sentences you dictated and
# what the app thinks you meant — the same record vocab.json is.
review.json
review.lock

# Saved web pages parked in the folder while testing the lookup and
# translate keys (ch/pp/cp_play/np_passport and friends). Like the logs
# above, they are a record of what you were reading — and they are not
# part of the app.
/*.html

# Pictures and videos OF THIS SCREEN. The most sensitive thing this repo
# can hold -- a screenshot can carry mail, banking, anything that was ever
# shown here -- and the same rule transcripts.log gets: it stays on this
# machine. The folder name is [capture] folder in config.toml; change that
# and change this.
captures/

# Generated at first run by cues.py
cues/

# The phone endpoint's shared secret: server_token.txt until 2026-09-17,
# since then a DPAPI blob under secrets\ (secretstore.py) — unreadable to
# any other Windows account, and still never committed.
server_token.txt
/secrets/

# The account's sync folder (sb.py, sync.py): what other PCs of the same
# account said, pulled here for the Said page, and the sync cursors.
/sync/

# Android build outputs and local toolchain paths
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
# The release keystore and the file that names it (plan 12.7): generated
# once, backed up twice, never committed — losing it is a new package
# identity for every user, leaking it is someone else signing as DeskIT.
android/keystore.properties
android/*.jks
android/*.keystore

# The first-run wizard has run on this copy (firstrun.py).
.setup-done

# awake.py: the marker that says the machine is being held awake and what
# to put back if the app dies holding it, and the timestamped record of
# every hold, release, screens-off and screens-on with what the probe found.
awake_state.json
awake.log
# ...and the names the same files had before 2026-09-03 (night.py),
# which an app started before the rename still writes.
night_state.json
night.log
# notify.py: every notification that arrived (titles and bodies from
# other programs) and the record of reminders and dismissals.
notify.json
notify.log

# problems.py: the owner's own bug list, which is the one store here
# that quotes him back to himself AND shows what was on his screen: a
# report carries the line he typed, the raw and final text of the
# dictation it is about, a pinned copy of the recording out of
# recent\, and a screenshot of the screen as it looked a moment
# before the box opened. That is transcripts.log and captures\ in one
# item, so it gets their rule: it stays on this machine. problems.md is
# regenerated from problems.json on every write — data, not a document
# anybody edits — and problems.lock is only the file the app and the
# dashboard take turns holding. The weekly review reads these local,
# untracked files by design; a fresh clone has an empty bug list
# rather than his.
problems.json
problems.lock
problems.md
problems/

# .claude\ is the project's own Claude Code folder and is COMMITTED on
# purpose: commands\weekly-reports.md IS the Saturday review routine,
# and a routine that only exists on one disk is one nobody can read.
# Only the per-machine leftovers are ignored — settings.local.json is
# this copy's permission answers, not a decision about the app.
.claude/settings.local.json

# paths.py (2026-09-17): the installed layout's scratch folders. A checkout
# never makes them (portable mode keeps the flat layout), but a DESKIT_HOME
# pointed at the checkout for a test would.
/cache/
/tmp/
# models.py / packs.py (chapter 6): the downloaded model and the
# wheel packs — an installed copy's, but `--download-model` in a
# checkout lands them here too.
/models/
/packs/
# The marker that keeps a copy in portable mode without a .git beside it.
/portable.txt

# The three layers (config.py, 2026-09-17): defaults.toml is TRACKED and
# never written by the app; these two are the person's and never leave the
# machine. config.toml / config.legacy.toml is the pre-layers file that
# --migrate reads once and retires.
/settings.toml
/settings.toml.bak
/state.json
# the consent rows (privacy.py): what the person allowed, when, which words
/consent.json
/consent.json.tmp
/config.toml
/config.legacy.toml

# the egress log net.py writes (D12): hosts and byte counts, no bodies
network.log*
# launch.spawn's record: one row per child it started, and whatever a
# child wrote to stderr before it died (the desk's import error, 1.1.0)
spawn.log*

# packaginguild_local.ps1's output: the wheelhouse, the python.org zip,
# the staged tree (~250 MB) and, with Inno Setup here, the installer
/dist/

# The Saturday routine's questions to the owner (questions.py) and the
# lock the app and the dashboard take turns holding — his answers, on
# his disk only, like problems.json above. .agents\ is the machine's
# own agent skills (not the app's; .gitattributes keeps it out of the
# build too). Chapter 16's row 0.4.
questions.json
questions.lock
.agents/

# the installer's pictures, drawn at build time (dev/make_wizard_images.py)
packaging/wizard/

# the master app keeps its ticks and its export ledger here (dev only)
dev/master/state/
dev/master/__pycache__/
dev/master/web/node_modules/
dev/master/web/dist/
